  "reason": "The current best (config_039, acc=0.7250) uses multimodal + multiprofile + scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. The only untested configuration that isolates a single variable from this best setup is config_038, which swaps weighted fusion for concat while keeping all other components identical. Evidence from config_032 vs config_033 (ResNet50) shows weighted > concat by ~2.5pp, but the ViT-L representation is substantially larger and may interact differently with the fusion strategy. As the final experiment, this completes the 2×2 fusion × image-encoder comparison at the known-optimal RNA/aggregation settings, confirming whether the weighted-fusion advantage holds with the stronger visual encoder or whether concat's simpler geometry might be competitive with ViT-L's richer features. It is the most informative single test remaining: it either confirms the current best is robust or reveals an unexpected fusion-image interaction that could shift the ranking."
